但我床尾也有一张长凳。

568
00:32:22.740 --> 00:32:23.800
No one sleeps on it.
没人会睡在上面。

569
00:32:23.960 --> 00:32:25.740
But this is a very popular thing.
但这其实很常见。

570
00:32:25.900 --> 00:32:29.540
I have an upholstered bench at the foot of my bed as well.
我床尾也有一张软垫长凳。

571
00:32:29.720 --> 00:32:31.740
It's where I like sort of lay my robe at night.
晚上我通常把睡袍放在那儿。

572
00:32:31.740 --> 00:32:33.240
You know, I like kick off my slippers.
你知道的，我喜欢把拖鞋踢掉。

573
00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:34.540
I put my robe on the bench.
把睡袍放在长凳上。

574
00:32:34.760 --> 00:32:34.920
Yeah.
是啊。

575
00:32:35.100 --> 00:32:36.460
And it's all there for me in the morning.
第二天早上一切都准备好了。

576
00:32:37.100 --> 00:32:39.820
My bench could not fit a grown man.
我的长凳可睡不下一个成年男人。

577
00:32:40.380 --> 00:32:41.880
It's a tiny little bench.
那是一张很小的长凳。

578
00:32:42.200 --> 00:32:46.660
I actually really looked at that bench and I was like, oh, they found a wide bench.
我当时真的看了那张长凳，心想，噢，他们找了一张很宽的长凳。

579
00:32:46.900 --> 00:32:48.340
That's a substantial bench.
那是一张很结实的长凳。

580
00:32:48.820 --> 00:32:49.680
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

581
00:32:50.120 --> 00:32:57.000
It's just big enough that you believe it, but still small enough that it's just so sad.
它大到让你觉得合理，但又小到让人觉得特别心酸。

582
00:32:57.000 --> 00:32:57.520
Yeah.
是啊。

583
00:32:57.800 --> 00:33:02.380
And also, just again, Michael has no space in his own home.
而且再说一次，迈克尔在自己家里一点空间都没有。

584
00:33:02.700 --> 00:33:08.960
She has both guest rooms she's using, and now he doesn't even get to sleep in his bed.
她把两间客房都占了，现在连床都不让他睡了。

585
00:33:08.980 --> 00:33:10.400
It's so sad.
太惨了。

586
00:33:10.600 --> 00:33:11.580
It's tragic.
简直是悲剧。

587
00:33:11.900 --> 00:33:13.720
And now I've got a fun fact.
现在我有个有趣的事实要分享。

588
00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:23.580
But this scene of the bedroom tour specifically, this scene is John McCain's favorite scene from the office.
关于卧室参观这一幕，这可是约翰·麦凯恩最喜欢的《办公室》片段。

589
00:33:23.900 --> 00:33:25.280
And I can tell you why.
我可以告诉你原因。

590
00:33:25.440 --> 00:33:25.600
Yeah.
好啊。

591
00:33:25.700 --> 00:33:26.400
How do you know that?
你怎么知道的？

592
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.840
That's such a random tidbit to know.
这消息也太冷门了吧。

593
00:33:29.380 --> 00:33:32.600
BJ Novak was at a dinner party with John McCain.
B.J.诺瓦克曾和约翰·麦凯恩一起参加过晚宴。

594
00:33:32.780 --> 00:33:36.040
I would love to hear that story, how that came about.
我很想听听那个故事，那是怎么发生的。

595
00:33:36.320 --> 00:33:37.840
That's fascinating to me.
这对我来说太有意思了。

596
00:33:37.980 --> 00:33:39.700
That's very on brand, though, for BJ.
不过这确实很符合B.J.的风格。

597
00:33:39.700 --> 00:33:43.880
BJ finds himself in these eclectic groups of people all the time.
B.J.总是能混进各种各样奇奇怪怪的圈子里。

598
00:33:44.040 --> 00:33:46.840
So this was, what, a few years ago, he's at a dinner party.
所以那是几年前的事了，他在参加一个晚宴。

599
00:33:47.020 --> 00:33:47.900
John McCain's there.
约翰·麦凯恩也在场。

600
00:33:48.380 --> 00:33:48.540
Yeah.
是啊。

601
00:33:48.700 --> 00:33:52.960
You want to be BJ's plus one to a dinner party because he's going to take you to a cool group.
你想做BJ参加晚宴的男伴，因为他会带你去见一个很酷的圈子。

602
00:33:53.220 --> 00:33:53.400
Yeah.
没错。

603
00:33:53.560 --> 00:33:57.000
He was at this dinner party, and someone walked up to him and said,
他当时在那个晚宴上，有人走过去对他说：

604
00:33:57.540 --> 00:33:59.720
John McCain is a huge fan of the office.
“约翰·麦凯恩是《办公室》的超级粉丝。”

605
00:33:59.720 --> 00:34:01.380
Would you like me to make an introduction?
“需要我为你引荐一下吗？”

606
00:34:01.820 --> 00:34:04.620
Now, I've experienced this, too, with politicians.
这种事我也在政客身上经历过。

607
00:34:04.620 --> 00:34:10.720
A lot of times, politicians, they have a person whose job it is to whisper things in their ears
很多时候，政客身边都有专门负责在他们耳边低语的人，

608
00:34:10.720 --> 00:34:16.520
that are really specific about the other guests at a party because they vetted everyone at the party
告诉他们关于宴会上其他客人的具体信息，因为他们已经对宴会上的每个人都做过背景调查，

609
00:34:16.520 --> 00:34:22.080
so that when the politician meets you, they can say something really specific and personal.
这样当政客见到你时，就能说出一些非常具体且私人的话。

610
00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:25.240
It's like the scene, you guys, in Devil Wears Prada, right?
就像《穿普拉达的女王》里的那个场景，对吧？

611
00:34:25.520 --> 00:34:27.220
Anne Hathaway is next to Meryl Streep.
安妮·海瑟薇站在梅丽尔·斯特里普旁边。

612
00:34:27.440 --> 00:34:32.140
They're at that big shindig in Paris, and she's telling her, every little person that walks up,
他们在巴黎参加那个大型派对，她告诉她，每一个走过来的人，

613
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:32.980
some little tidbit.
都有什么小八卦。

614
00:34:32.980 --> 00:34:33.740
Yes.
是的。

615
00:34:34.060 --> 00:34:41.000
So BJ was like, oh, he's probably been told, I work on this show called The Office and yada yada.
所以BJ心想，哦，他大概是被告知了，我在一部叫《办公室》的剧里工作，诸如此类的。

616
00:34:41.180 --> 00:34:46.600
So BJ was like, I'm going to put him to the test, and I'm going to ask him specifically,
于是BJ决定，我要考验他一下，我要专门问他：

617
00:34:47.380 --> 00:34:51.800
John McCain, tell me one of your favorite scenes from The Office.
“约翰·麦凯恩，告诉我一个你最喜欢的《办公室》片段。”

618
00:34:52.080 --> 00:34:52.460
BJ.
BJ啊。

619
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:53.760
Right?
对吧？

620
00:34:54.400 --> 00:34:55.380
My gosh.
天哪。

621
00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:55.840
Okay.
好吧。

622
00:34:56.240 --> 00:34:58.620
So when he met him, he did it.
所以当他见到他时，他真的这么做了。

623
00:34:58.780 --> 00:35:01.040
He said, what's one of your favorite scenes?
他问：“你最喜欢的片段是哪一个？”

624
00:35:01.040 --> 00:35:08.560
And John McCain said, I love that scene in the dinner party when they're given the house tour,
约翰·麦凯恩回答说，我喜欢《晚宴》那一集，他们参观房子的时候，

625
00:35:08.560 --> 00:35:13.900
and they walk into the bedroom, and the video camera's up in the background, and the bench.
走进卧室，背景里有摄像机，还有那个长凳。

626
00:35:14.020 --> 00:35:20.020
And he just went on and on with such great detail that BJ knew, oh, this is for real.
他滔滔不绝地说了那么多细节，BJ就知道，哦，这是真的。

627
00:35:20.020 --> 00:35:21.520
This guy does love The Office.
这家伙是真的喜欢《办公室》。

628
00:35:21.960 --> 00:35:23.160
That's so wild.
太疯狂了。

629
00:35:23.420 --> 00:35:24.800
It's so specific.
太具体了。

630
00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:25.420
Yeah.
是啊。

631
00:35:25.420 --> 00:35:27.040
It's such a specific scene.
那确实是一个很具体的片段。

632
00:35:27.440 --> 00:35:28.280
It was.
确实。

633
00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:32.640
Well, he picked a good episode, and he picked a good scene, because when I was re-watching this
嗯，他选了一集好戏，也选了一个好片段，因为当我跟我丈夫李重温这一集时，

634
00:35:32.640 --> 00:35:37.200
with my husband, Lee, this was the scene where I thought we were going to have to pause,
这一幕让我觉得我们得暂停一下，

635
00:35:37.240 --> 00:35:38.820
because he couldn't catch his breath.
因为他笑得喘不过气来。

636
00:35:38.820 --> 00:35:40.640
He was, like, laughing so hard.
他当时笑得太厉害了。

637
00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:43.960
All right.
好吧。

638
00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:48.440
Well, speaking of having to, like, pause to catch your breath, because you're laughing so hard,
说到因为笑得太厉害而不得不暂停喘口气，

639
00:35:48.440 --> 00:35:52.900
Jenna, up next is the scene with the tiny TV.
珍娜，接下来就是那个小电视的片段了。

640
00:35:53.480 --> 00:35:54.420
Oh, my God.
天哪。

641
00:35:54.600 --> 00:35:59.020
The tiny plasma TV that only comes out two inches from the wall.
那个离墙面只有两英寸的小等离子电视。

642
00:35:59.810 --> 00:36:05.780
There are two times when I laughed so hard on our show that I thought I wasn't going to ever
我们在拍这部剧时，有两次我笑得太厉害，以为自己永远都

643
00:36:05.780 --> 00:36:06.260
recover.
缓不过来了。

644
00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:09.080
This was one of them.
这就是其中之一。

645
00:36:09.380 --> 00:36:11.520
Tears streaming down our face.
我们当时泪流满面。

646
00:36:11.520 --> 00:36:16.400
We had a fan question from Matty S, Paula T, Kennedy H.
我们收到了来自Matty S、Paula T和Kennedy H的粉丝提问。

647
00:36:16.740 --> 00:36:22.220
How many takes did you guys have to do when Michael was showing off his plasma TV?
迈克尔展示他的等离子电视时，你们拍了多少条？

648
00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:25.980
Guys, John Krasinski talks about this.
伙计们，约翰·卡拉辛斯基谈到了这一点。

649
00:36:26.240 --> 00:36:27.680
I'm going to turn it over to him.
我要把时间交给他。

650
00:36:28.810 --> 00:36:35.040
When we got to the moment with the television, I think there was an energy in the room that was
当我们拍到电视那一幕时，我觉得房间里的气氛是

651
00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:35.580
overwhelming.
太震撼了。

652
00:36:35.780 --> 00:36:38.900
I was already quaking with laughter.
我当时已经笑得浑身发抖了。

653
00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:41.340
It wouldn't have taken much for me to laugh.
其实我本来就很容易笑场。

654
00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:46.880
And then throw in maybe one of my favorite jokes in the entire show.
再加上这可能是我整部剧里最喜欢的笑话之一。

655
00:36:47.140 --> 00:36:49.740
And I remember at the table, read laughing.
我记得在围读剧本的时候，我就已经在笑了。

656
00:36:50.020 --> 00:36:58.000
But then to see Steve again with that beaming face of pride, just turn to us and say,
但看到史蒂夫那张洋溢着自豪的脸，转过头对我们说，

657
00:36:58.120 --> 00:37:01.820
you won't believe what I have.
你们绝对想不到我有什么好东西。

658
00:37:01.860 --> 00:37:06.580
And also, look what it can do when company comes over.
而且，看看有客人来的时候它能做什么。

659
00:37:06.740 --> 00:37:08.040
I can just do this.
我只要这样就行了。

660
00:37:08.040 --> 00:37:16.240
And I'm pretty sure that the distance between the TV and the wall was like an inch and a half.
我敢肯定电视机和墙之间的距离也就一英寸半左右。

661
00:37:16.400 --> 00:37:21.480
And he was so proud that it comes out to watch TV in the comfort of your own home.
他当时特别自豪，觉得这样就能在家里舒舒服服地看电视了。

662
00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:28.240
And then you push it back a good inch and a half to hide it away when company comes.
然后有客人来的时候，再把它往回推个一英寸半藏起来。

663
00:37:28.540 --> 00:37:32.080
Luckily, the outtakes are out there in the world.
好在这些花絮现在已经公之于众了。

664
00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:35.120
And so you can see, I mean, Jenna can tell you.
你们可以去看看，我是说，珍娜可以告诉你们。

665
00:37:35.260 --> 00:37:44.280
But I think that it took probably 19 or 20 takes before I was even able to stand up vertically
我觉得大概拍了十九二十次，我才终于能站直了，

666
00:37:44.940 --> 00:37:47.600
in that scene without doubling over.
在那场戏里没笑弯腰。

667
00:37:48.120 --> 00:37:50.440
And again, as I've always said, I'm a crier laugher.
再说一次，我一直都说，我笑起来会哭。

668
00:37:50.680 --> 00:37:54.160
So when I laugh that hard, my entire face turns red with tears.
所以我笑得那么厉害时，整张脸都会涨红，眼泪直流。

669
00:37:54.580 --> 00:38:00.380
And the pressure that's filling in my face for trying not to laugh and to no avail.
那种因为努力憋笑而充血的感觉，根本没用。

670
00:38:00.600 --> 00:38:03.000
I don't know why I even try not to laugh.
我不知道我为什么要努力憋笑。

671
00:38:03.120 --> 00:38:04.320
I should just let it out.
我应该直接笑出来的。

672
00:38:04.320 --> 00:38:07.080
And then my face wouldn't turn beet red in every scene.
那样我的脸就不会在每一场戏里都涨成猪肝色了。

673
00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:10.400
That is without a doubt one of my favorite scenes.
那绝对是我最喜欢的场景之一。

674
00:38:10.400 --> 00:38:14.480
And I will cherish that memory for the rest of my career.
我会把那段回忆珍藏在我的整个职业生涯中。

675
00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:20.440
You can hear him losing it, just retelling it, you know?
你听他讲的时候，自己都快笑场了，对吧？

676
00:38:21.060 --> 00:38:21.420
Yes.
没错。

677
00:38:22.100 --> 00:38:27.680
Well, Jenna, one of my daughter's favorite things since we've been doing Office Ladies
珍娜，自从我们开始做《办公室女郎》以来，我女儿最喜欢的事情之一

678
00:38:27.680 --> 00:38:30.040
is watching the bloopers.
就是看花絮。

679
00:38:30.400 --> 00:38:33.080
My daughter, Isabel, absolutely loves them.
我女儿伊莎贝尔特别喜欢这些花絮。

680
00:38:33.220 --> 00:38:34.840
She watches them over and over.
她一遍又一遍地看。

681
00:38:34.840 --> 00:38:40.320
I think it's so fun for her to see you and I laughing and these people that she's known,
我觉得对她来说，看到你和我大笑，看到这些她从出生起就认识的人，

682
00:38:40.320 --> 00:38:43.020
you know, since she was born, cracking up.
笑得前仰后合，真的很有趣。

683
00:38:43.200 --> 00:38:47.300
So she actually helped me gather all the bloopers for this episode.
所以她这次帮我收集了这一集所有的花絮。

684
00:38:47.460 --> 00:38:48.640
She knew right where they were.
她清楚地知道它们在哪里。

685
00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:50.860
She even knew time codes, Jenna.
她甚至连时间码都知道，珍娜。

686
00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:52.160
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

687
00:38:52.220 --> 00:38:55.140
You're passing along the love of time codes to Isabel.
你把对时间码的热爱传给了伊莎贝尔。

688
00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:56.040
I am.
确实传给她了。

689
00:38:56.040 --> 00:39:01.020
So I feel like we have to hear the blooper of this scene because it's so wonderful.
我觉得我们必须听听这场戏的花絮，因为它太精彩了。

690
00:39:01.340 --> 00:39:02.760
Sam, can you play that?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

691
00:39:02.760 --> 00:39:07.040
I guess what surround sound means is that, right over here, Jenna.
我想环绕立体声的意思是，就在这儿，珍娜。

692
00:39:10.860 --> 00:39:11.940
Two speakers.
两个扬声器。

693
00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:13.840
Damn.
该死。

694
00:39:14.540 --> 00:39:15.360
We have two speakers.
我们有两个扬声器。

695
00:39:16.100 --> 00:39:16.740
What?
什么？

696
00:39:17.340 --> 00:39:17.940
Honey?
亲爱的？

697
00:39:18.420 --> 00:39:19.020
Oh, Jesus.
天哪。

698
00:39:19.560 --> 00:39:21.040
This is terrible.
这太糟糕了。

699
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:22.800
Never finish this episode.
这集永远也拍不完了。

700
00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:24.640
Um, check this out.
嗯，看看这个。

701
00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:25.840
Folds.
折叠。

702
00:39:39.540 --> 00:39:49.440
Lady, Eve did a whole runner where they just let him go with this TV.
天哪，史蒂夫演得太绝了，他们就这么让他带着这台电视走了。

703
00:39:49.840 --> 00:39:50.120
Oh, man.
噢，天哪。

704
00:39:50.480 --> 00:39:54.180
And he tries to explain that the TV has surround sound.
他还试图解释说这台电视有环绕立体声。

705
00:39:54.440 --> 00:40:00.160
And what he means by that is that the screen is surrounded by a speaker.
他所谓的意思是，屏幕周围围了一圈扬声器。

706
00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:11.540
The whole thing was, you've gone to someone's house when they've just gotten their new TV system with their new sound speakers, and they're so excited to show it off.
整件事的背景是，你去别人家做客，他们刚买了新的电视系统和音响，兴奋地想向你展示。

707
00:40:11.640 --> 00:40:15.100
Maybe they even, like, play part of a movie for you, right?
也许他们还会给你放一段电影，对吧？

708
00:40:15.360 --> 00:40:15.720
Yes.
没错。

709
00:40:15.880 --> 00:40:17.600
That was the inspiration for this.
这就是这段戏的灵感来源。

710
00:40:17.720 --> 00:40:23.560
And so Steve was going to bring that energy of, like, we were sitting in a professionally done.
所以史蒂夫想要营造出那种感觉，就好像我们坐在一个专业的……

711
00:40:24.620 --> 00:40:26.000
Home theater, right?
家庭影院里，对吧？

712
00:40:26.640 --> 00:40:27.040
Yes.
对。

713
00:40:27.520 --> 00:40:32.620
But instead, he's just talking about this tiny TV, which, by the way, is not even a plasma TV.
但实际上，他只是在谈论这台小电视，顺便说一句，它甚至不是等离子电视。

714
00:40:32.820 --> 00:40:36.420
It's just a flat screen TV, but it keeps referring to it as a plasma TV.
它只是一台平板电视，但他一直管它叫等离子电视。

715
00:40:36.860 --> 00:40:37.840
Oh, my God.
天哪。

716
00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:39.700
Jenna, do you know what I love?
珍娜，你知道我最喜欢什么吗？

717
00:40:39.820 --> 00:40:43.100
Is that how this is still a joke with the caSt.
就是这个梗在演员群里到现在还很火。

718
00:40:43.360 --> 00:40:46.020
So a few years ago, you guys, we've talked about this before.
几年前，大家伙儿，我们之前聊过这个。

719
00:40:46.180 --> 00:40:52.160
We have a cast text thread where we will text and check in, say hello, little clips, pictures of our kids.
我们有个演员群，大家会在里面聊天、问候、发些小视频和孩子的照片。

720
00:40:52.160 --> 00:40:59.100
And Creed usually sings us a song at Christmas, and he'll text us, you know, him at home with his, like, elf hat on.
克里德通常会在圣诞节给我们唱歌，他会发短信给我们，你知道，就是他在家戴着精灵帽的样子。

721
00:40:59.820 --> 00:41:02.520
And Jenna sent a photo to all of us.
然后珍娜给咱们所有人都发了一张照片。

722
00:41:02.600 --> 00:41:11.000
You were on a job, and you walked into, like, a little dressing room they had for you, and there was the tiniest TV mounted on the wall.
当时你在工作，走进他们为你准备的小更衣室，墙上挂着一台超级小的电视。

723
00:41:11.180 --> 00:41:14.360
Jenna, and you sent us a picture, and we all started cracking up.
珍娜，你发了那张照片，我们全都笑疯了。

724
00:41:14.540 --> 00:41:15.020
Yes.
没错。

725
00:41:15.020 --> 00:41:21.280
I walked into this dressing room, and I thought to myself, you could hold this in your hand.
我走进那个更衣室，心想，这玩意儿我单手都能拿住。

726
00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:23.840
Why have they mounted it on the wall?
为什么还要把它挂在墙上？

727
00:41:24.100 --> 00:41:28.100
It was so reminiscent of the dinner party episode.
这太让人想起《晚宴》那一集了。

728
00:41:28.480 --> 00:41:32.600
I was so excited to send that text, and people were loving it.
我当时特别兴奋地发了那条短信，大家都很喜欢。

729
00:41:32.760 --> 00:41:34.940
It will never get old to me, that scene.
那个场景我永远看不腻。

730
00:41:35.040 --> 00:41:37.000
I can watch it and watch it and watch it.
我可以一遍又一遍地看。

731
00:41:37.120 --> 00:41:42.060
But there are so many things in this living room that made me laugh on a second watch, Jenna.
但珍娜，二刷的时候，客厅里还有好多东西让我笑个不停。

732
00:41:42.060 --> 00:41:50.420
And I also remembered it the day we were filming, because I was seated by it, that janky side table that Michael made.
我还记得拍摄那天，因为我就坐在那张迈克尔做的破烂边桌旁边。

733
00:41:51.060 --> 00:41:53.520
It is the saddest-looking table.
那张桌子看起来太寒酸了。

734
00:41:55.720 --> 00:41:58.260
It looks like scrap wood.
看起来就像废木料做的。

735
00:41:58.440 --> 00:42:03.400
Like, if you got a crate of firewood, that he used the crate to make the table.
就像是用装柴火的板条箱拼凑出来的桌子。

736
00:42:03.680 --> 00:42:05.820
And the dialogue cracked me up, too.
而且那段对话也让我笑喷了。

737
00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.200
Jim is like, is that chestnut?
吉姆问，那是栗木吗？

738
00:42:07.200 --> 00:42:10.740
And he's like, I think it's either pine or Nordic cherry.
他说，我觉得是松木或者北欧樱桃木。

739
00:42:11.080 --> 00:42:11.940
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么鬼？

740
00:42:14.680 --> 00:42:17.940
Angela, it's time for you to arrive at this dinner party.
安吉拉，你该去参加这场晚宴了。

741
00:42:18.120 --> 00:42:20.400
Oh, Andy and Angela, here we come.
噢，安迪和安吉拉，我们来了。

742
00:42:20.640 --> 00:42:23.020
We had a fan question from Haley M.
我们有一个来自海莉·M的粉丝提问。

743
00:42:23.300 --> 00:42:28.820
Angela, are you starting to break when Michael goes in for the hug, which you refuse?
安吉拉，当迈克尔想要拥抱你而你拒绝时，你是不是快要憋不住笑了？

744
00:42:28.820 --> 00:42:29.760
Yes.
是的。

745
00:42:30.380 --> 00:42:30.980
Yes.
没错。

746
00:42:31.300 --> 00:42:37.220
I pretty much, like John said, the minute I walked in that room and saw everything, just
就像约翰说的，我一走进那个房间，看到这一切，几乎是……

747
00:42:37.220 --> 00:42:41.220
the minute we started those scenes, I was already tickled.
我们一开始拍那些戏，我就已经被逗乐了。

748
00:42:41.360 --> 00:42:44.800
And everything from then on was just me trying not to laugh.
从那以后，我所做的一切就是努力不让自己笑场。

749
00:42:45.000 --> 00:42:48.260
I have a fun catch at 6 minutes, 34 seconds.
我在6分34秒处发现了一个有趣的穿帮。

750
00:42:48.560 --> 00:42:56.940
When Andy takes off his coat, underneath his coat, he is wearing a turtleneck with a shirt
当安迪脱下外套时，外套里面他穿了一件高领毛衣和一件衬衫。

751
00:42:56.940 --> 00:43:01.760
over it, and then a sweater tied around his neck.
搞定了，脖子上还系着一件毛衣。

752
00:43:01.980 --> 00:43:02.680
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

753
00:43:02.780 --> 00:43:04.380
He's in prime preppy mode.
他现在是典型的学院风打扮。

754
00:43:04.640 --> 00:43:07.920
This was a bit that Gene, our writer, came up with.
这是我们的编剧吉恩想出的一个桥段。

755
00:43:08.040 --> 00:43:13.240
He just thought it would be really, really funny to have a person who has tied a sweater
他觉得让一个脖子上系着毛衣的人

756
00:43:13.240 --> 00:43:15.780
around their neck take their coat off.
脱掉外套会非常非常搞笑。

757
00:43:15.860 --> 00:43:16.160
Yeah.
没错。

758
00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:18.340
He had that ready to go underneath.
他早就准备好穿在里面了。

759
00:43:19.000 --> 00:43:23.220
Well, you know, I said I would let you guys know when we had some belly hiding.
嗯，你们知道的，我说过会告诉你们什么时候有遮挡孕肚的镜头。

760
00:43:23.760 --> 00:43:28.100
It's happening all through the episode, but one of my favorites is this giant bouquet of
整集里都有这种情况，但我最喜欢的一个是这束巨大的

761
00:43:28.100 --> 00:43:28.520
flowers.
鲜花。

762
00:43:28.900 --> 00:43:30.360
That was to hide my belly.
那是为了遮住我的肚子。

763
00:43:30.560 --> 00:43:30.940
Yes.
是的。

764
00:43:31.100 --> 00:43:32.340
That's how big my belly is.
我的肚子就是那么大。

765
00:43:32.480 --> 00:43:34.160
Look at that bouquet of flowers.
看看那束花。

766
00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:40.920
They had to make the bouquet that big because the point of it was for Andy to give his hostess
他们必须把花束做得那么大，因为剧情需要安迪送给女主人

767
00:43:40.920 --> 00:43:41.700
some flowers.
一些花。

768
00:43:41.700 --> 00:43:45.560
But the reason they're so large was because they were a belly hide.
但它们之所以那么大，是因为要用来遮肚子。

769
00:43:45.940 --> 00:43:50.000
There's a great blooper from this as well, if you guys go back and rewatch them.
这里还有一个很棒的NG镜头，如果你们回去重看的话。

770
00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:53.240
But I have a little catch I want to point out.
但我有一个小发现想提一下。

771
00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:54.220
What is it?
是什么？

772
00:43:54.500 --> 00:44:00.080
At six minutes, 44 seconds, I'm standing next to Jan while Andy's doing the tuna, tuna.
在6分44秒的时候，我站在简旁边，当时安迪正在唱“金枪鱼，金枪鱼”。

773
00:44:00.260 --> 00:44:01.420
Bet you get a lot of tuna.
打赌你一定吃了不少金枪鱼。

774
00:44:01.560 --> 00:44:02.180
You eat a lot of tuna.
你吃了很多金枪鱼。

775
00:44:02.300 --> 00:44:02.820
That whole bit.
就是那整段戏。

776
00:44:03.180 --> 00:44:03.580
Yep.
没错。

777
00:44:03.700 --> 00:44:09.540
I just, as an actor, just my own little prep that I decided to do was I just stared at
作为一名演员，我当时自己做了一个小小的准备，就是我一直盯着

778
00:44:09.540 --> 00:44:10.160
Jan's boobs.
简的胸部看。

779
00:44:10.360 --> 00:44:11.940
I mean, I was eye level to them.
我是说，我的视线正好和它们平齐。

780
00:44:12.060 --> 00:44:12.680
She's in heels.
她穿着高跟鞋。

781
00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:13.600
She's taller than me.
她比我高。

782
00:44:13.720 --> 00:44:14.360
They're right there.
它们就在那儿。

783
00:44:14.360 --> 00:44:19.580
And I decided to throw her a little judgy shade, Angela Martin sass look.
于是我决定给她一个评头论足的眼神，那种安吉拉·马丁式的傲慢表情。

784
00:44:19.880 --> 00:44:23.700
And Paul Feig came up to me and was like, oh, my gosh, Angela, I just caught in camera
保罗·费格走过来对我说，天哪，安吉拉，我刚才在镜头里捕捉到

785
00:44:23.700 --> 00:44:26.920
that you're giving Jan's boobs the judgy look.
你在用那种审视的眼神看简的胸部。

786
00:44:27.060 --> 00:44:28.680
He was like, you got to do that every time.
他说，你每次都得这么演。

787
00:44:28.860 --> 00:44:29.700
So I did.
所以我照做了。

788
00:44:29.860 --> 00:44:30.840
And it made it in the show.
而且这一幕还被剪进了正片里。

789
00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:35.460
And it's just one of those little moments that wasn't scripted that ends up on the screen.
这就是那些没写在剧本里，却最终出现在屏幕上的小瞬间之一。

790
00:44:35.460 --> 00:44:37.460
And it's always fun to relive those.
重温这些时刻总是很有趣。

791
00:44:37.640 --> 00:44:40.860
But that is a big, of course, Angela would do that moment.
但这确实是一个非常“安吉拉当然会这么做”的时刻。

792
00:44:41.120 --> 00:44:41.980
Like, of course.
没错，当然。

793
00:44:42.220 --> 00:44:42.360
Right.
对。

794
00:44:42.360 --> 00:44:43.780
I'm so glad they caught it.
我很高兴他们捕捉到了这一幕。

795
00:44:44.060 --> 00:44:49.380
This is also when we find out, Angela, that the ossobucco will not be ready for at least
这也是我们发现的时候，安吉拉，炖牛膝至少还要

796
00:44:49.380 --> 00:44:50.020
three hours.
三个小时才能做好。

797
00:44:50.020 --> 00:44:56.140
And I love Pam's line when she says, do you mean three hours from now or like three hours
我很喜欢帕姆说的那句台词，她说，你是说从现在起三个小时，还是说从

798
00:44:56.140 --> 00:44:58.440
from four o'clock when you started it?
你四点钟开始做的时候算起三个小时？

799
00:44:58.920 --> 00:45:04.240
Jenna, when I rewatched the scene, that is one of the lines that you say that is most like
珍娜，当我重看这一幕时，那句台词是你说的最像

800
00:45:04.240 --> 00:45:05.540
you in real life.
现实生活中你的台词之一。

801
00:45:05.720 --> 00:45:06.400
It is.
确实是。

802
00:45:06.580 --> 00:45:10.760
It just felt like in that moment, Jenna was saying it as your friend.
当时的感觉就是，珍娜是以你朋友的身份在说那句话。

803
00:45:10.760 --> 00:45:11.820
I was like, that would be Jenna.
我就想，那确实是珍娜会说的话。

804
00:45:11.820 --> 00:45:14.160
She'd be like, no, but you planned ahead.
她会说，不，但你提前计划好了。

805
00:45:14.360 --> 00:45:14.740
Surely.
当然。

806
00:45:15.020 --> 00:45:19.520
If you know it takes three hours, surely you had already estimated the time that you'd
如果你知道这需要三个小时，那你肯定已经预估好了

807
00:45:19.520 --> 00:45:20.300
be serving it.
上菜的时间。

808
00:45:20.720 --> 00:45:24.640
I feel like that is something I could possibly say.
我觉得那可能确实是我会说的话。

809
00:45:24.780 --> 00:45:25.240
Yes.
没错。

810
00:45:25.340 --> 00:45:26.700
In response to a hoSt.
作为对主人的回应。

811
00:45:26.940 --> 00:45:28.680
Sometimes in Spain, they eat at midnight.
在西班牙，人们有时会在午夜进餐。

812
00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:30.420
So when in Rome.
所以入乡随俗嘛。

813
00:45:31.040 --> 00:45:32.120
When in Rome.
入乡随俗。

814
00:45:32.580 --> 00:45:35.960
I guess we're going to sit around and drink some wine now.
我想我们现在得坐下来喝点酒了。

815
00:45:36.220 --> 00:45:37.520
Michael makes a toaSt.
迈克尔敬了一杯酒。

816
00:45:37.520 --> 00:45:41.020
He notes the Okie afterbirth of the wine.
他提到了那款酒有股俄克拉荷马州的余味。

817
00:45:41.240 --> 00:45:44.200
Jean told me that Steve improvised that line.
简告诉我那句台词是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

818
00:45:44.500 --> 00:45:45.100
You're kidding.
你开玩笑吧。

819
00:45:45.720 --> 00:45:46.900
Okie afterbirth.
俄克拉荷马州的余味。

820
00:45:47.020 --> 00:45:47.840
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

821
00:45:48.040 --> 00:45:48.940
Steve Carell.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

822
00:45:49.320 --> 00:45:52.920
Well, now Jan needs to relax.
好吧，现在简需要放松一下。

823
00:45:53.300 --> 00:45:55.060
She wants to put some music on.
她想放点音乐。

824
00:45:55.440 --> 00:45:55.780
Yeah.
是啊。

825
00:45:55.780 --> 00:46:02.880
And I don't know if you know this, but her former assistant, Hunter, is a fabulous musician.
我不知道你知不知道，但她以前的助理亨特是一位出色的音乐家。

826
00:46:03.280 --> 00:46:05.800
And so she's going to put on his CD.
所以她打算放他的CD。

827
00:46:05.980 --> 00:46:06.920
It's called The Hunted.
专辑名叫《被猎杀者》。

828
00:46:07.620 --> 00:46:07.940
Yeah.
没错。

829
00:46:08.160 --> 00:46:12.060
And then she's going to dance by herself in front of all of us.
然后她要在我们所有人面前独自跳舞。

830
00:46:14.080 --> 00:46:16.300
We got some fan mail about that.
我们收到了一些关于那段戏的粉丝来信。

831
00:46:16.500 --> 00:46:23.220
Amanda B, Ileana B, and Gabe G said, please tell us everything about Jan's dance.
阿曼达·B、伊莱亚娜·B和盖比·G说，请告诉我们关于简跳舞的所有细节。

832
00:46:23.520 --> 00:46:25.000
Well, I'll start with this.
好吧，我先从这点说起。

833
00:46:25.460 --> 00:46:31.400
Jean told me that after we did a few takes of Melora dancing on her own, he had the idea
简告诉我，在我们拍了几条梅洛拉独自跳舞的镜头后，他有个想法，

834
00:46:31.400 --> 00:46:34.360
that she should try to pull Jim into the dance.
就是让她试着把吉姆也拉进舞池。

835
00:46:34.560 --> 00:46:37.860
So he got her aside and he gave her that note privately.
于是他把她叫到一边，私下里给了她这个建议。

836
00:46:38.200 --> 00:46:40.700
John did not know that was going to happen.
约翰当时并不知道会发生这种事。

837
00:46:40.700 --> 00:46:43.240
And Melora just ran with it.
而梅洛拉直接就照做了。

838
00:46:43.440 --> 00:46:45.500
And we didn't know either.
我们当时也不知道。

839
00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:49.620
And Jenna, when I rewatched that now, knowing that, right?
珍娜，我现在重看那段戏时，知道了这一点，对吧？

840
00:46:49.780 --> 00:46:51.280
Because Jean shared that with you.
因为简跟你分享过。

841
00:46:51.400 --> 00:46:53.240
And then Melora talked to me about it.
然后梅洛拉也跟我聊过这件事。

842
00:46:53.400 --> 00:46:57.740
I watched our faces, not only John's, but I watched yours and mine because it was a surprise
我观察了我们的表情，不仅是约翰的，还有你和我的，因为这对我们三个人来说都是个惊喜。

843
00:46:57.740 --> 00:46:58.700
to all three of us.
对我们三个人来说都是。

844
00:46:58.820 --> 00:47:03.940
And you can really see a look on both of our faces of like, what's happening?
你真的能从我们俩的脸上看出那种“到底发生了什么？”的表情。

845
00:47:05.060 --> 00:47:06.120
It was perfect.
那真是太完美了。

846
00:47:06.820 --> 00:47:10.040
Well, like Angela said, we did ask Melora about this.
嗯，就像安吉拉说的，我们确实问过梅洛拉这件事。

847
00:47:10.040 --> 00:47:12.980
And she told us the inspiration behind her dancing.
她告诉了我们她跳舞背后的灵感来源。

848
00:47:13.360 --> 00:47:21.060
One of the most fun moments to play was the dancing with John Krasinski for the song that
表演中最有趣的时刻之一就是和约翰·卡拉辛斯基一起跳那首亨特写的歌。

849
00:47:21.060 --> 00:47:21.800
Hunter had written.
亨特写的。

850
00:47:22.060 --> 00:47:28.500
It just felt like such a wonderful sort of jab at Michael, you know, so passive aggressive.
感觉就像是对迈克尔的一种绝妙的讽刺，你知道，那种被动攻击。

851
00:47:28.500 --> 00:47:30.380
And also, I'm a dancer.
而且，我还是个舞者。

852
00:47:30.560 --> 00:47:34.840
So I really wanted to just be a little like off the beat.
所以我真的很想让自己看起来有点跟不上节奏。

853
00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:40.560
I wanted to make sure that I really tried hard to just be so inappropriate, but also just like a
我想确保自己真的努力表现得非常不得体，但同时又有点

854
00:47:40.560 --> 00:47:44.640
little bit off the beat, a little drunk, kind of a little tipsy.
跟不上节奏，有点醉醺醺的，带点微醺的感觉。

855
00:47:44.760 --> 00:47:49.140
And I felt like that would be even a better, you know, even a better jab to Michael because
我觉得那样会更好，你知道，对迈克尔来说会是更沉重的一击，因为

856
00:47:49.140 --> 00:47:52.120
Jen and Michael are like at war at that point in the episode.
在那一集里，简和迈克尔正处于交战状态。

857
00:47:54.000 --> 00:47:56.460
I love that she's a little off the beat.
