00:56:01.810 --> 00:56:08.850
And it sort of was like a mental chess match between Jim and Pam and that Pam ends up winning.
那就像是吉姆和帕姆之间的一场心理博弈，最后是帕姆赢了。

1004
00:56:09.190 --> 00:56:13.250
And they thought Pam was the victor of this scene.
他们认为帕姆是这场戏的赢家。

1005
00:56:13.390 --> 00:56:18.090
But people could not get past the fact that for a moment, Jim was willing to leave her there.
但人们无法接受这样一个事实：那一刻，吉姆竟然愿意把她留在那儿。

1006
00:56:18.670 --> 00:56:21.110
Well, that should tell you how bad the night was going.
嗯，这足以说明那天晚上有多糟糕了。

1007
00:56:21.790 --> 00:56:25.350
It didn't really bump me because he included you in the beginning.
我倒没觉得有什么不妥，因为他一开始是带上你了。

1008
00:56:25.430 --> 00:56:29.530
It's only when he was challenged that he was like, okay, well, I'm gone.
只是当他受到质疑时，他才表现出，好吧，那我就走了。

1009
00:56:29.530 --> 00:56:34.850
Well, the evening has now dissolved into just silence.
好吧，现在整个晚上都陷入了死一般的寂静。

1010
00:56:35.450 --> 00:56:38.710
It's just everyone sitting around saying nothing.
大家只是坐在那儿，什么话也不说。

1011
00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:42.730
And how long have they been sitting there just in silence?
他们在那儿沉默地坐了多久了？

1012
00:56:43.310 --> 00:56:44.290
I don't know.
我不知道。

1013
00:56:44.630 --> 00:56:48.590
I mean, Jan is fully reclined with her head back and her eyes closed.
我是说，简整个人向后靠着，头仰着，眼睛闭着。

1014
00:56:50.650 --> 00:56:52.630
Well, Pam gets a little chilly.
嗯，帕姆觉得有点冷。

1015
00:56:52.790 --> 00:56:55.130
So Michael offers her his jacket.
所以迈克尔把他的外套给了她。

1016
00:56:55.430 --> 00:56:55.870
Oof.
噢。

1017
00:56:56.470 --> 00:56:58.010
And this sets off Jan.
这下惹恼了简。

1018
00:56:58.010 --> 00:57:01.190
This scene is so brilliant.
这一幕真是太精彩了。

1019
00:57:01.750 --> 00:57:03.590
Melora and Steve are so amazing.
梅洛拉和史蒂夫演得太棒了。

1020
00:57:03.950 --> 00:57:14.050
But her look, the look Melora gives you and then slowly glances back over to Michael and then glances back to Pam.
但她的眼神，梅洛拉看向你，然后慢慢瞥向迈克尔，又瞥回帕姆的那种眼神。

1021
00:57:14.250 --> 00:57:22.770
And then you see her thinking and planning to say something embarrassing about him.
然后你能看到她在思考，计划着要说些让他难堪的话。

1022
00:57:22.770 --> 00:57:31.890
The story Jan tells is that she's very sorry it's so chilly, but they're having to have their sliding door replaced.
简讲的故事是说，她很抱歉屋里这么冷，但他们不得不更换推拉门。

1023
00:57:31.890 --> 00:57:34.350
And you can see a big blue tarp over the door.
你可以看到门上盖着一块巨大的蓝色防水布。

1024
00:57:34.750 --> 00:57:41.150
And the reason is because Michael ran through the glass when he heard the ice cream truck.
原因就是迈克尔听到冰淇淋车的声音时，直接撞穿了玻璃。

1025
00:57:41.890 --> 00:57:42.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1026
00:57:42.550 --> 00:57:44.090
Jan's like, it's a cute story.
简觉得这故事挺可爱的。

1027
00:57:44.250 --> 00:57:47.370
Michael ran through the sliding glass doors because he thought he heard the ice cream truck.
迈克尔撞穿了推拉玻璃门，因为他以为自己听到了冰淇淋车的声音。

1028
00:57:47.530 --> 00:57:48.770
And Michael's like, stop it.
迈克尔说，别说了。

1029
00:57:48.890 --> 00:57:49.870
I don't like the story.
我不喜欢这个故事。

1030
00:57:50.250 --> 00:57:50.710
Okay, fine.
好吧，行。

1031
00:57:50.790 --> 00:57:51.670
Look, I like ice cream.
听着，我喜欢冰淇淋。

1032
00:57:51.670 --> 00:57:52.290
So sue me.
去告我吧。

1033
00:57:52.410 --> 00:57:56.630
And then he's like, wait, I shouldn't say that because she will sue you because she loves lawsuits.
然后他又说，等等，我不该这么说，因为她真的会告你，她就爱打官司。

1034
00:57:57.230 --> 00:58:01.810
And then he said the glass was extremely clean.
接着他说那块玻璃当时特别干净。

1035
00:58:02.230 --> 00:58:03.950
And it was like it was invisible.
干净得就像隐形了一样。

1036
00:58:04.150 --> 00:58:08.130
And she just erupts.
然后她就爆发了。

1037
00:58:08.450 --> 00:58:09.770
She's like, you're so right.
她说，你说得太对了。

1038
00:58:09.870 --> 00:58:10.410
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

1039
00:58:10.410 --> 00:58:13.410
Because before I lived here, the glass was always covered in smudges.
因为我住进来之前，那玻璃上总是布满污渍。

1040
00:58:13.430 --> 00:58:14.970
And then I moved in and I cleaned it.
然后我搬进来，把它擦干净了。

1041
00:58:15.050 --> 00:58:16.470
So I guess that makes me the devil.
所以我想这让我成了恶魔。

1042
00:58:16.470 --> 00:58:21.870
And then they're both like crazy laughing with like crazy eyes.
然后他们两个都疯狂地大笑起来，眼神都变得很疯狂。

1043
00:58:21.870 --> 00:58:24.670
And he's like, yeah, she is the devil.
他说，没错，她就是恶魔。

1044
00:58:24.890 --> 00:58:25.790
And it is.
确实如此。

1045
00:58:26.170 --> 00:58:27.530
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1046
00:58:27.530 --> 00:58:30.050
It's two people unhinged.
这是两个精神失常的人。

1047
00:58:30.730 --> 00:58:33.830
Here's what Gene told me about this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，吉恩是这么跟我说这场戏的。

1048
00:58:33.830 --> 00:58:41.050
He told me that the theme of this episode was, quote, dinner party from hell.
他告诉我，这一集的主题是“地狱般的晚宴”。

1049
00:58:41.250 --> 00:58:45.850
And the idea was that Michael is in hell and Jan is the devil.
其构思是迈克尔身处地狱，而简就是恶魔。

1050
00:58:46.130 --> 00:58:46.350
Oh.
噢。

1051
00:58:46.350 --> 00:58:50.090
And so they did a lot of things toward this theme.
所以他们围绕这个主题做了很多设计。

1052
00:58:50.290 --> 00:58:55.610
For example, they designed Malora's wardrobe so that she was dressed in red.
比如，他们给马洛拉设计了服装，让她穿上红色的衣服。

1053
00:58:55.750 --> 00:58:59.950
And for this scene where they wrote that line, I guess I'm the devil.
在写那句台词的场景里，我猜我就是那个魔鬼。

1054
00:59:00.210 --> 00:59:02.790
And then, you know, Michael responds, and I'm in hell.
然后，你知道，迈克尔回应了，我就身处地狱之中。

1055
00:59:03.510 --> 00:59:06.870
They purposely placed her in front of a roaring fire.
他们特意把她安排在熊熊燃烧的火炉前。

1056
00:59:07.030 --> 00:59:12.630
And then in the room, they have all of her candles lit all around Michael so that he does
在房间里，他们点燃了她周围所有的蜡烛，围在迈克尔身边，让他看起来

1057
00:59:12.630 --> 00:59:15.250
appear to be in the flames of hell.
仿佛置身于地狱的烈火之中。

1058
00:59:15.250 --> 00:59:21.770
But Malora improvised that moment where she made little devil horns on her head, which is
但马洛拉即兴发挥，在头上比出了小恶魔角的动作，这真的

1059
00:59:21.770 --> 00:59:23.850
so, so funny.
太搞笑了。

1060
00:59:24.090 --> 00:59:29.290
But yeah, if you look around this apartment, there's a ton of red stuff.
不过确实，如果你环顾这间公寓，会发现到处都是红色的东西。

1061
00:59:29.530 --> 00:59:30.630
There is.
确实如此。

1062
00:59:30.790 --> 00:59:37.950
And, you know, I caught at 11 minutes, five seconds, that red pot-like thing that she took
而且，你知道，我在11分05秒的时候注意到，那个红色的锅状物，就是她

1063
00:59:37.950 --> 00:59:41.750
when she was fired in the job and it dropped out of the box and they had to put it back
被解雇时从盒子里掉出来的那个，他们不得不把它放回

1064
00:59:41.750 --> 00:59:42.230
in the box.
盒子里。

1065
00:59:42.230 --> 00:59:45.390
It's seated next to her on the little table.
它就放在她旁边的小桌子上。

1066
00:59:46.130 --> 00:59:47.010
Amazing detail.
细节太棒了。

1067
00:59:47.410 --> 00:59:50.530
We're about to go into the kitchen for some girls' time.
我们马上要进厨房享受闺蜜时光了。

1068
00:59:50.770 --> 00:59:53.930
And in the kitchen, all of her cookware is red.
在厨房里，她所有的厨具都是红色的。

1069
00:59:54.370 --> 00:59:55.750
All of that was on purpose.
这一切都是刻意安排的。

1070
00:59:56.190 --> 00:59:58.430
Well, let's talk about this kitchen scene.
好吧，我们来聊聊这个厨房场景。

1071
00:59:58.890 --> 01:00:00.970
Pam has wanted to break up the tension in the room.
帕姆想打破房间里紧张的气氛。

1072
01:00:01.110 --> 01:00:02.230
She's like, is there more wine?
她说，还有酒吗？

1073
01:00:02.430 --> 01:00:03.890
And Jen's like, no, no, no, I'll get it.
珍说，不，不，不，我去拿。

1074
01:00:03.950 --> 01:00:05.370
No, actually, let's have some girl time.
不，其实，我们来享受一下闺蜜时光吧。

1075
01:00:05.790 --> 01:00:06.510
Angela, come on.
安吉拉，来吧。

1076
01:00:06.510 --> 01:00:08.410
And she takes them into the kitchen.
然后她把她们带进了厨房。

1077
01:00:08.830 --> 01:00:12.870
Well, Jenna, there were a few scenes that we filmed, us three gals, in this kitchen.
珍娜，我们三个女孩在这个厨房里拍了好几场戏。

1078
01:00:13.130 --> 01:00:14.950
Only one made it into the episode.
只有一场被剪进了正片。

1079
01:00:15.190 --> 01:00:16.830
But there is another one.
但还有另一场。

1080
01:00:16.830 --> 01:00:17.910
And it's great.
而且非常棒。

1081
01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:19.310
Sam, can you play it?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

1082
01:00:20.530 --> 01:00:25.390
So, this girl that I basically grew up with becomes Miss West Virginia.
那个我从小一起长大的女孩成了西弗吉尼亚小姐。

1083
01:00:25.670 --> 01:00:28.250
And then suddenly, all the boys start paying attention to me.
然后突然间，所有的男孩都开始关注我了。

1084
01:00:28.930 --> 01:00:35.190
And it was funny because I never even considered myself beautiful until people started pointing
这很有趣，因为我从来没觉得自己漂亮，直到人们开始

1085
01:00:35.190 --> 01:00:35.770
it out to me.
指出来。

1086
01:00:36.230 --> 01:00:41.070
They were like, Jan, wow, you are so much more beautiful than Miss West Virginia.
他们说，简，哇，你比西弗吉尼亚小姐漂亮多了。

1087
01:00:42.150 --> 01:00:47.030
Oh, so that is why I, um, wait, Pam, what was your, what was your question?
噢，所以这就是为什么我，嗯，等等，帕姆，你的，你的问题是什么？

1088
01:00:47.270 --> 01:00:48.050
Where did you grow up?
你在哪里长大的？

1089
01:00:49.930 --> 01:00:50.410
Incredible.
太不可思议了。

1090
01:00:51.150 --> 01:00:52.350
Isn't it so good?
是不是很棒？

1091
01:00:52.810 --> 01:00:53.210
Yeah.
是啊。

1092
01:00:53.490 --> 01:00:56.110
She just goes off about Miss West Virginia.
她一直在喋喋不休地讲西弗吉尼亚小姐的事。

1093
01:00:56.110 --> 01:00:59.170
And we're just sitting there in silence as she's chopping things.
而我们只是坐在那里沉默不语，看着她切东西。

1094
01:00:59.370 --> 01:01:01.310
She clearly hates this woman.
她显然很讨厌那个女人。

1095
01:01:01.730 --> 01:01:04.450
My question was, where did you grow up?
我的问题是，你在哪里长大的？

1096
01:01:04.690 --> 01:01:04.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1097
01:01:05.430 --> 01:01:10.290
And in the kitchen scene, you'll notice I'm standing behind a little ledge by the counter.
在厨房那场戏里，你会注意到我站在柜台边的一个小台子后面。

1098
01:01:10.290 --> 01:01:14.830
And I remember Paul Feig and I were so excited that there was a ledge in the kitchen.
我记得保罗·费格和我当时非常兴奋，因为厨房里有个台子。

1099
01:01:15.050 --> 01:01:16.310
They didn't have to build that.
他们不需要专门搭建那个。

1100
01:01:16.450 --> 01:01:19.670
And I fit perfectly tucked into it so we could hide my belly.
我刚好可以躲在后面，这样就能遮住我的肚子。

1101
01:01:19.870 --> 01:01:24.830
Well, while the ladies are having their time in the kitchen, Michael gives the guys a tour
嗯，当女士们在厨房里聚会时，迈克尔带着男士们参观了

1102
01:01:24.830 --> 01:01:25.710
of the garage.
车库。

1103
01:01:25.990 --> 01:01:31.270
He also uses this time to try to get them to invest in Serenity by Jan.
他还趁这段时间试图说服他们投资“简的宁静”蜡烛公司。

1104
01:01:31.590 --> 01:01:32.210
And he's in.
而且他加入了。

1105
01:01:32.470 --> 01:01:34.910
You don't need to say more than a sentence to him.
你对他甚至不需要多说一句话。

1106
01:01:35.170 --> 01:01:39.350
This is my daughter's favorite line in the whole episode is when he goes,
这是我女儿在整集里最喜欢的一句台词，就是当他说，

1107
01:01:39.350 --> 01:01:40.230
thought about it.
考虑过了。

1108
01:01:40.510 --> 01:01:40.830
I'm in.
我加入。

1109
01:01:41.890 --> 01:01:47.050
Michael's like, do you want to invest $10,000 into this candle business?
迈克尔就像是说，你想投资一万美元到这个蜡烛生意里吗？

1110
01:01:47.270 --> 01:01:48.230
Think about it.
考虑一下。

1111
01:01:48.490 --> 01:01:49.390
Thought about it.
考虑过了。

1112
01:01:49.510 --> 01:01:49.970
I'm in.
我加入。

1113
01:01:50.810 --> 01:01:55.370
Well, when we asked Ed about his memories from shooting the dinner party,
嗯，当我们问埃德关于拍摄那场晚宴的回忆时，

1114
01:01:55.650 --> 01:01:59.270
he talked about the first time he saw this garage.
他谈到了第一次看到这个车库的情景。

1115
01:01:59.750 --> 01:02:01.190
Sam, can you play that clip?
萨姆，你能播放那段片段吗？

1116
01:02:02.370 --> 01:02:06.030
At some point while we were shooting, I stepped off the set.
拍摄期间有一次，我走出了片场。

1117
01:02:06.030 --> 01:02:09.910
I think I was probably just going to get a snack or something at craft service.
我想我当时可能只是去剧组餐车拿点零食之类的。

1118
01:02:10.050 --> 01:02:13.390
And I watched through the garage of the condo where we were shooting.
我透过我们拍摄的那间公寓的车库往里看。

1119
01:02:13.630 --> 01:02:16.730
And the garage was also a location in the episode.
那个车库也是这一集里的一个取景地。

1120
01:02:16.910 --> 01:02:19.110
They had done all the set decoration for the garage.
他们已经完成了车库所有的布景装饰。

1121
01:02:19.110 --> 01:02:25.770
And I noticed this amazing detail in there, which is that all of the items in Michael Scott's garage
我注意到里面有一个非常惊人的细节，就是迈克尔·斯科特车库里的所有物品

1122
01:02:25.770 --> 01:02:31.450
were things that he had bought from infomercials, like late night infomercials.
都是他从电视购物节目里买来的，就是那种深夜电视购物。

1123
01:02:31.450 --> 01:02:35.150
And this was just like a background joke in the show.
这只是剧中的一个背景笑话。

1124
01:02:35.410 --> 01:02:40.710
Like, I remember seeing like a Bowflex and like a meat dehydrator, like all this random stuff.
比如，我记得看到了像Bowflex健身器和肉类脱水机之类的，全是这种乱七八糟的东西。

1125
01:02:40.710 --> 01:02:46.870
And it just made me laugh so hard and was such a reminder of how incredible the office team was.
这让我笑得不行，也提醒了我《办公室》团队是多么不可思议。

1126
01:02:47.090 --> 01:02:52.150
Everyone at every level from production design, set decoration, all those details,
每个人，从制作设计到布景装饰，每一个层级，所有那些细节，

1127
01:02:52.370 --> 01:02:57.850
all of those people that worked on the show were so creative and contributing to the comedy of that show
所有参与这部剧的人都非常有创意，他们以各种或大或小的方式

1128
01:02:57.850 --> 01:03:00.790
in very big and very small ways.
为这部剧的喜剧效果做出了贡献。

1129
01:03:00.790 --> 01:03:03.090
And it all made such a difference.
这一切都产生了巨大的影响。

1130
01:03:03.470 --> 01:03:06.090
Anyway, that's one of my favorite details about that episode.
总之，那是关于那一集我最喜欢的细节之一。

1131
01:03:07.350 --> 01:03:09.690
Angela, I looked it up.
安吉拉，我查过了。

1132
01:03:10.090 --> 01:03:14.290
So currently a Bowflex system starts around $1,500.
目前一套Bowflex系统起价大约是1500美元。

1133
01:03:15.090 --> 01:03:20.190
But Michael had both a Bowflex and a Soloflex.
但迈克尔既有Bowflex又有Soloflex。

1134
01:03:20.730 --> 01:03:23.830
And a Soloflex is like $2,400.
而Soloflex大概要2400美元。

1135
01:03:24.990 --> 01:03:32.910
And then like Ed said, like meat dehydrator, just any as-seen-on-TV item was shoved into the space.
就像埃德说的，还有肉类脱水机，任何电视购物上看到的东西都被塞进了那个空间里。

1136
01:03:33.090 --> 01:03:34.970
And really pricey stuff.
而且都是些很贵的东西。

1137
01:03:34.970 --> 01:03:39.370
There's two boxes of La Cousette, like Dutch ovens.
还有两箱La Cousette，就是那种荷兰锅。

1138
01:03:39.530 --> 01:03:41.170
Those are so expensive.
那些非常贵。

1139
01:03:41.810 --> 01:03:43.430
They're like at Williams-Sonoma.
它们是在威廉姆斯-索诺玛那种店里卖的。

1140
01:03:43.610 --> 01:03:47.530
And it just kind of is that reminder of when Oscar sat down with him and said,
这让人想起奥斯卡坐下来问他时说的话，

1141
01:03:47.570 --> 01:03:48.510
what are you buying?
你都在买些什么？

1142
01:03:48.650 --> 01:03:50.250
What are you spending your money on?
你把钱都花在什么上面了？

1143
01:03:50.250 --> 01:03:57.030
And I don't know if you noticed, but there's also just boxes labeled Michael's stuff.
我不知道你有没有注意到，那里还有写着“迈克尔的东西”的箱子。

1144
01:03:57.390 --> 01:03:57.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
01:03:57.910 --> 01:04:02.470
So clearly Jan went through and just boxed up a bunch of his stuff.
所以很明显，简把他的东西都打包整理出来了。

1146
01:04:02.470 --> 01:04:04.550
And it's out there living in the garage.
现在它们就住在车库里。

1147
01:04:04.630 --> 01:04:05.530
So sad.
真可怜。

1148
01:04:05.810 --> 01:04:06.130
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1149
01:04:06.290 --> 01:04:09.690
You know the two chairs by that fireplace were those two hand seats.
你知道壁炉旁的那两把椅子是那两张手型椅吗？

1150
01:04:10.810 --> 01:04:11.730
That's right.
没错。

1151
01:04:11.990 --> 01:04:14.470
But those aren't in the living room anymore.
但那些东西已经不在客厅里了。

1152
01:04:15.190 --> 01:04:16.990
Lady, I think we should take a break.
女士，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

1153
01:04:16.990 --> 01:04:20.230
We still have so much more to talk about.
我们还有很多话要聊呢。

1154
01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:21.290
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1155
01:04:21.530 --> 01:04:24.350
Dwight and the babysitter haven't even showed up yet.
德怀特和保姆甚至还没到呢。

1156
01:04:24.590 --> 01:04:27.390
Well, we will get to that right after this break.
好吧，休息过后我们马上就会聊到那一点。

1157
01:04:38.300 --> 01:04:39.220
Ding dong.
叮咚。

1158
01:04:41.520 --> 01:04:43.740
Oh, there's two more guests.
哦，又来了两位客人。

1159
01:04:44.340 --> 01:04:45.440
Jan is confused.
简很困惑。

1160
01:04:45.860 --> 01:04:47.360
Her whole dinner party is here.
她的晚宴宾客全到齐了。

1161
01:04:47.620 --> 01:04:48.860
Michael is not.
迈克尔却没到。

1162
01:04:49.080 --> 01:04:50.540
He knows who's at the door.
他知道门口是谁。

1163
01:04:50.840 --> 01:04:57.060
It's Dwight and Melvina, his older babysitter from when he was a child.
是德怀特和梅尔维娜，他小时候的保姆。

1164
01:04:57.060 --> 01:04:58.460
Oh, and don't worry.
哦，别担心。

1165
01:04:58.680 --> 01:05:01.920
They've brought two wine glasses and a cooler of food.
他们带了两个红酒杯和一个装食物的冷藏箱。

1166
01:05:02.040 --> 01:05:02.420
Yeah.
没错。

1167
01:05:02.600 --> 01:05:04.900
Since they're unexpected, they've got it covered.
既然是不速之客，他们都准备好了。

1168
01:05:05.120 --> 01:05:05.560
Don't worry.
别担心。

1169
01:05:05.820 --> 01:05:07.200
And two lawn chairs.
还有两把折叠椅。

1170
01:05:07.860 --> 01:05:09.840
So they have a place to sit.
这样他们就有地方坐了。

1171
01:05:10.100 --> 01:05:13.100
The wine glasses are the biggest ones you'll ever see.
那红酒杯大得让你难以置信。

1172
01:05:13.440 --> 01:05:14.520
Yes, they are.
确实如此。

1173
01:05:14.900 --> 01:05:16.480
This sets off an argument.
这引发了一场争吵。

1174
01:05:16.940 --> 01:05:21.580
Jan wants Michael to send them away, but Michael stands his ground.
简想让迈克尔把他们打发走，但迈克尔坚持己见。

1175
01:05:22.310 --> 01:05:22.560
Yeah.
没错。

1176
01:05:22.880 --> 01:05:28.760
Michael's like, listen, you said he couldn't come because he didn't have a plus one or we
迈克尔的态度是，听着，你说他不能来是因为他没有带女伴，或者我们

1177
01:05:28.760 --> 01:05:29.740
didn't have enough wine glasses.
没有足够的红酒杯。

1178
01:05:29.900 --> 01:05:32.180
Well, he brought the wine glasses and he brought another human.
好吧，他带了红酒杯，还带了另一个人来。

1179
01:05:32.440 --> 01:05:33.100
I know.
我知道。

1180
01:05:33.100 --> 01:05:33.800
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1181
01:05:33.980 --> 01:05:35.240
He's brought a person.
他带了一个人来。

1182
01:05:35.380 --> 01:05:35.960
A person.
一个人。

1183
01:05:36.420 --> 01:05:37.560
So here we go.
所以，我们开始吧。

1184
01:05:37.840 --> 01:05:40.820
And Jan is like, fine, have it your way.
简说，行，随你的便。

1185
01:05:40.960 --> 01:05:43.160
And Michael's like, have it my way.
迈克尔说，随我的便？

1186
01:05:43.320 --> 01:05:46.100
When do things ever go my way?
我的事什么时候随过我的便？

1187
01:05:46.360 --> 01:05:46.840
Yeah.
没错。

1188
01:05:46.840 --> 01:05:50.780
When he wanted to see Stomp and she wanted to see Wicked, what did they see?
当他想看《破铜烂铁》而她想看《女巫前传》时，他们看了什么？

1189
01:05:51.140 --> 01:05:51.580
Wicked.
《女巫前传》。

1190
01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:56.100
When she said she wasn't ready to have children, what did Michael do?
当她说还没准备好要孩子时，迈克尔做了什么？

1191
01:05:56.260 --> 01:05:57.260
He had a vasectomy.
他做了输精管结扎手术。

1192
01:05:57.480 --> 01:05:59.280
Then she decided, I want kids.
后来她决定，我想要孩子。

1193
01:05:59.440 --> 01:06:00.980
He had the vasectomy reversed.
他又做了输精管复通手术。

1194
01:06:01.240 --> 01:06:02.720
But then she changed her mind again.
但后来她又改变了主意。

1195
01:06:02.720 --> 01:06:04.320
He had another vasectomy.
他又做了一次结扎手术。

1196
01:06:04.600 --> 01:06:06.100
Sip, snap, sip, snap, sip, snap.
剪断，接上，剪断，接上，剪断，接上。

1197
01:06:06.540 --> 01:06:10.820
Do you know the physical toll that three vasectomies takes on a person?
你知道三次输精管手术对一个人的身体伤害有多大吗？

1198
01:06:11.700 --> 01:06:16.060
Oh, all of this happens in front of all of us.
哦，这一切都是在我们所有人面前发生的。

1199
01:06:16.060 --> 01:06:19.100
There is so much to unpack about this scene, guys.
伙计们，这一幕有太多东西值得深挖了。

1200
01:06:19.420 --> 01:06:20.320
So buckle in.
所以，系好安全带吧。

1201
01:06:20.600 --> 01:06:25.260
I mean, when we saw The Bench, we thought it can't get weirder than The Bench.
我的意思是，当我们看到《长椅》那一集时，我们以为不会有比那更离谱的了。

1202
01:06:25.540 --> 01:06:28.880
And then we played Celebrity.
然后我们又演了《名人》那一集。

1203
01:06:29.220 --> 01:06:36.420
And now we're standing in the hallway of the condo yelling about vasectomies?
现在我们竟然站在公寓走廊里大喊大叫讨论输精管切除术？

1204
01:06:36.660 --> 01:06:38.020
Where can it go?
还能再离谱到什么程度？

1205
01:06:38.720 --> 01:06:43.060
Let's start with Dwight's date, his former babysitter, Melvina.
我们先从德怀特的约会对象说起，也就是他以前的保姆梅尔维娜。

1206
01:06:43.060 --> 01:06:49.580
Angela Jean told me that they thought it would be really fun to offer this role to our longtime
安吉拉·简告诉我，他们觉得让我们的长期选角导演艾莉森·琼斯来演这个角色会非常有趣。

1207
01:06:49.580 --> 01:06:51.900
casting director, Alison Jones.
但她拒绝了。

1208
01:06:52.140 --> 01:06:53.480
But she said no.
她拒绝了。

1209
01:06:53.840 --> 01:06:54.880
She refused.
她拒绝了。

1210
01:06:57.100 --> 01:07:02.620
Greg wanted the incredible Beth Grant to play the role.
格雷格想让了不起的贝丝·格兰特来演这个角色。

1211
01:07:02.920 --> 01:07:03.460
Well, yes.
嗯，没错。

1212
01:07:03.620 --> 01:07:07.040
Greg had worked with Beth before and knew her very well.
格雷格以前和贝丝合作过，非常了解她。

1213
01:07:07.040 --> 01:07:11.460
You guys might recognize her from the film No Country for Old Men.
你们可能在电影《老无所依》中见过她。

1214
01:07:11.680 --> 01:07:13.340
I mean, she has a huge filmography.
我的意思是，她的演艺履历非常丰富。

1215
01:07:13.540 --> 01:07:16.380
But at this time, that film had just come out.
但当时那部电影才刚刚上映。

1216
01:07:16.800 --> 01:07:18.380
We reached out to Beth.
我们联系了贝丝。

1217
01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:24.620
And she told us the story of exactly how she was cast on the show.
她向我们讲述了她是如何被选中出演这个角色的。

1218
01:07:24.620 --> 01:07:33.080
I was thrilled when I got the call to do this part and to be Rain's babysitter and girlfriend.
接到电话让我演这个角色，还要当雷恩的保姆兼女友，我当时兴奋极了。

1219
01:07:35.100 --> 01:07:37.800
It's demented, and I love it.
这设定太疯狂了，我喜欢。

1220
01:07:37.940 --> 01:07:42.560
And I had worked with Steve Carell fairly recently in Little Miss Sunshine.
而且我最近刚和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在《阳光小美女》里合作过。

1221
01:07:42.560 --> 01:07:46.580
So I was already completely in love with him and did love the show.
所以我已经完全迷上他了，而且我也很喜欢这部剧。

1222
01:07:46.580 --> 01:07:50.180
And I had worked with Greg Daniels on King of the Hill.
我还和格雷格·丹尼尔斯在《乡巴佬希尔》里合作过。

1223
01:07:50.180 --> 01:07:53.700
And we ran into each other during the Writer's Guild strike.
我们在编剧工会罢工期间偶遇了。

1224
01:07:54.000 --> 01:07:56.360
And I think he saw me in my strike mode.
我想他当时看到了我处于罢工状态的样子。

1225
01:07:56.360 --> 01:08:00.320
I guess he knew I was right to be able to be that demented woman.
我想他知道我有能力演好那个疯狂的女人。

1226
01:08:02.760 --> 01:08:07.920
Well, then Beth shares with us what it was like to do the scene at the front door.
那么，贝丝和我们分享了她在前门拍那场戏时的感受。

1227
01:08:08.060 --> 01:08:10.060
She's holding a cooler the whole time.
她全程都拎着一个冷藏箱。

1228
01:08:10.180 --> 01:08:11.520
This is all happening.
这一切都在发生着。

1229
01:08:11.680 --> 01:08:14.120
It's her first scene of the episode.
这是她那一集里的第一场戏。

1230
01:08:14.420 --> 01:08:15.660
Here's what she had to say.
听听她是怎么说的。

1231
01:08:15.660 --> 01:08:21.000
Coming to the door to that dinner party was so thrilling for me.
能去那场晚宴开门，我感到非常激动。

1232
01:08:21.180 --> 01:08:23.360
It was so hard not to laugh.
忍住不笑真的太难了。

1233
01:08:23.780 --> 01:08:27.160
I felt that since I knew Steve, he was out to get me.
我觉得因为我认识史蒂夫，他就是想整我。

1234
01:08:27.320 --> 01:08:28.560
He wanted me to break.
他想让我笑场。

1235
01:08:28.740 --> 01:08:33.240
And here I was, a guest star, nervous with all you regulars, you fabulous comedians,
而我当时只是个客串演员，面对你们这些常驻演员，这些了不起的喜剧演员，我感到很紧张，

1236
01:08:33.560 --> 01:08:36.020
you brilliant comic minds.
你们这些才华横溢的喜剧大脑。

1237
01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:39.180
And here I am, the guest star with Rain.
而我，作为客串演员，正和雷恩在一起。

1238
01:08:39.440 --> 01:08:43.300
And opening the door is Steve Carell, just going for it.
开门的是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，他简直是火力全开。

1239
01:08:43.300 --> 01:08:48.840
And I started this riff and improvising to the point that I was determined not to laugh.
我开始即兴发挥，当时我下定决心绝对不能笑场。

1240
01:08:48.920 --> 01:08:51.700
So I started almost grunting and crying.
所以我开始发出类似咕哝和哭泣的声音。

1241
01:08:54.200 --> 01:08:58.800
I don't know if you can hear it in the episode, but, and tears in my eyes.
我不知道你们在剧里能不能听出来，但我当时眼里确实含着泪水。

1242
01:08:58.860 --> 01:09:00.040
And he said, oh, great.
他说，哦，太棒了。

1243
01:09:00.200 --> 01:09:01.600
Now she's crying or something.
她现在哭起来了还是怎么着。

1244
01:09:01.740 --> 01:09:03.160
And I leaned over.
然后我俯下身去。

1245
01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:06.460
I was holding that cooler, you know, bringing our own food.
我当时拎着那个冷藏箱，你知道的，自带食物。

1246
01:09:06.460 --> 01:09:09.800
And since we weren't invited, holding that cooler.
因为我们没被邀请，所以拎着那个冷藏箱。

1247
01:09:10.020 --> 01:09:13.560
And I leaned over, just shaking all over and came back up.
我俯下身，浑身颤抖，然后又直起身来。

1248
01:09:13.660 --> 01:09:16.200
And somehow I think I managed not to break.
不知怎么的，我想我成功忍住没笑场。

1249
01:09:16.340 --> 01:09:21.320
But that was the only time I managed not to break because you guys were just so hilarious.
但那是我唯一一次成功忍住没笑场，因为你们实在太搞笑了。

1250
01:09:21.960 --> 01:09:27.940
Jenna, we should share with everyone what line Steve improvised that sent us all to the floor.
珍娜，我们应该和大家分享一下史蒂夫即兴说出的那句台词，当时把我们所有人都逗得前仰后合。

1251
01:09:27.940 --> 01:09:33.720
Yes, guys, Steve improvised the line, snip, snap, snip, snap.
没错，各位，那句“咔嚓、咔嚓、咔嚓、咔嚓”是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

1252
01:09:33.980 --> 01:09:38.500
You have no idea the physical toll three vasectomies has on a person.
你们根本不知道做三次输精管结扎手术对身体的伤害有多大。

1253
01:09:38.900 --> 01:09:45.700
I mean, you try not laughing with Steve Carell in front of you improvising stuff like that.
我是说，面对史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在那儿即兴发挥，你根本没法忍住不笑。

1254
01:09:45.880 --> 01:09:47.220
We were all a goner.
我们当时全都破功了。

1255
01:09:47.520 --> 01:09:51.860
Well, it's interesting because Paul Feig sent in an audio clip about this,
嗯，这很有趣，因为保罗·费格发来了一段关于此事的音频片段，

1256
01:09:51.980 --> 01:09:53.420
and I'll let him explain it.
我就让他来解释吧。

1257
01:09:53.520 --> 01:09:56.800
But there's a reason why Steve improvised that line.
但史蒂夫即兴说出那句台词是有原因的。

1258
01:09:56.800 --> 01:09:57.760
Here you go.
给你听听。

1259
01:09:58.400 --> 01:10:01.520
There's so many great things to think about and remember from this episode.
这一集里有很多值得回味和铭记的精彩瞬间。

1260
01:10:01.680 --> 01:10:05.460
But the one that makes me just realize how genius Steve Carell is,
但让我意识到史蒂夫·卡瑞尔有多天才的那一个瞬间，

1261
01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:08.260
in case anybody didn't realize that already,
以防还有人没意识到这一点，

1262
01:10:09.260 --> 01:10:12.960
is when the whole snip, snap run was,
就是那段“咔嚓、咔嚓”的戏份，

1263
01:10:13.080 --> 01:10:18.220
it was a pretty dramatic scene of them, like, talking about having kids and all this.
当时那场戏其实挺沉重的，他们在那儿讨论生孩子之类的话题。

1264
01:10:18.340 --> 01:10:20.320
And so we did several takes of it.
我们拍了好几个版本。

1265
01:10:20.420 --> 01:10:22.000
It was really good, but it was very dramatic.
效果确实很好，但太严肃了。

1266
01:10:22.220 --> 01:10:24.000
And I remember kind of saying to Steve,
我记得我当时跟史蒂夫说，

1267
01:10:24.800 --> 01:10:27.460
maybe let's do a take or just kind of find a little more humor in it.
也许我们可以试着拍一版，稍微加点幽默感进去。

1268
01:10:27.560 --> 01:10:30.020
I know it's kind of hard because it's kind of a serious subject.
我知道这很难，因为这毕竟是个严肃的话题。

1269
01:10:30.240 --> 01:10:31.380
And he's like, oh, okay, yeah, I get it.
他说，哦，好的，没问题，我明白了。

1270
01:10:31.460 --> 01:10:31.660
I get it.
我明白了。

1271
01:10:31.700 --> 01:10:34.940
And that's when he did it, went off on the whole snip, snap, snip, snap,
然后他就开始表演了，即兴发挥了那段“咔嚓、咔嚓、咔嚓、咔嚓”，

1272
01:10:35.500 --> 01:10:36.420
which is just brilliant.
简直太绝了。

1273
01:10:36.580 --> 01:10:39.580
I mean, that scene is so funny because it's so heartbreaking and cringy,
我是说，那场戏之所以那么好笑，是因为它既让人心碎又让人尴尬，

1274
01:10:39.660 --> 01:10:40.760
but also hilarious.
但同时也非常搞笑。

1275
01:10:41.360 --> 01:10:43.080
I remember that, Angela.
我记得那场戏，安吉拉。

1276
01:10:43.300 --> 01:10:48.360
I remember doing takes and takes of that scene where they were just going back and forth.
我记得我们拍了一遍又一遍，他们在那儿来回争执。

1277
01:10:48.560 --> 01:10:52.540
And you could just see the pain and Michael that he wasn't a father
你能看出迈克尔因为没能当上父亲而感到的痛苦，

1278
01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:55.520
and that Jan had been so manipulative of him.
也能看出简对他有多么操纵控制。

1279
01:10:55.660 --> 01:10:57.240
And it was like a drama.
那简直就像是一部正剧。

1280
01:10:57.480 --> 01:10:59.920
And then Paul came over and talked to Steve.
然后保罗走过来跟史蒂夫谈了谈。

1281
01:11:00.300 --> 01:11:03.940
And they were like, how can we make this a comedy again?
他们当时在想，怎么才能让这重新变成喜剧呢？

1282
01:11:04.240 --> 01:11:07.620
How can we keep the dark elements of this scene,
我们该如何保留这场戏的黑暗元素，

1283
01:11:07.620 --> 01:11:09.900
but not let it get too heavy?
同时又不让它显得太沉重？

1284
01:11:10.400 --> 01:11:11.760
Brilliant Steve Carell.
天才史蒂夫·卡瑞尔。

1285
01:11:12.000 --> 01:11:14.340
Yeah, he so saves the moment.
没错，他真的拯救了那一刻。

1286
01:11:14.340 --> 01:11:15.400
And it's hilarious.
而且非常搞笑。

1287
01:11:15.700 --> 01:11:16.600
I mean, you're cringing.
我是说，你会觉得尴尬。

1288
01:11:16.600 --> 01:11:17.460
It's horrible.
太糟糕了。

1289
01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:20.280
It's, but he makes it funny.
但他是真的把它变得好笑了。

1290
01:11:20.980 --> 01:11:21.440
Yeah.
没错。

1291
01:11:21.720 --> 01:11:24.320
Well, now, guys, we're going to sit down at the table.
好了，各位，我们要坐到桌边去了。

1292
01:11:24.580 --> 01:11:26.240
I guess dinner is ready.
我想晚餐准备好了。

1293
01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:27.580
Near ready.
快好了。

1294
01:11:27.860 --> 01:11:28.340
Finally.
终于。

1295
01:11:28.920 --> 01:11:30.600
Can I point something out?
我能指出一点吗？

1296
01:11:30.880 --> 01:11:31.100
Yeah.
说吧。

1297
01:11:31.360 --> 01:11:35.860
If you look at the table, we all have wine glasses, right?
如果你看桌子，我们每个人都有红酒杯，对吧？

1298
01:11:35.860 --> 01:11:42.000
We also all have water glasses, which are wine glasses.
我们每个人还有水杯，但那其实也是红酒杯。

1299
01:11:42.620 --> 01:11:50.360
So clearly Jan had more than six wine glasses because she is using them for water as well.
所以很明显，简准备的红酒杯不止六个，因为她连喝水都用红酒杯。

1300
01:11:50.500 --> 01:11:54.780
She just didn't want Dwight to come, you guys, to her fancy party.
她只是不想让德怀特来参加她那场高级派对，伙计们。

1301
01:11:54.780 --> 01:11:56.940
He did not make the liSt.
他没能上榜。

1302
01:11:57.380 --> 01:12:00.180
Well, Dwight has started eating.
嗯，德怀特已经开始吃了。

1303
01:12:00.500 --> 01:12:01.800
I mean, they brought their own food.
我是说，他们自带了食物。

1304
01:12:01.960 --> 01:12:03.220
They're wasting no time.
他们真是一点时间都不浪费。

1305
01:12:03.520 --> 01:12:05.020
They're the only ones eating.
只有他们在吃。

1306
01:12:05.020 --> 01:12:08.420
Jan is still upset over what happened at the door.
简还在为门口发生的事心烦。

1307
01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:10.900
She's so upset, she has to excuse herself.
她心烦到必须找借口离开。

1308
01:12:11.040 --> 01:12:11.920
She goes to the kitchen.
她去了厨房。

1309
01:12:12.260 --> 01:12:12.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1310
01:12:12.700 --> 01:12:17.800
I mean, the last thing she said before she sat at that dining table was, I hate my life.
我是说，她在餐桌前坐下前说的最后一句话是：我讨厌我的生活。

1311
01:12:18.380 --> 01:12:18.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1312
01:12:19.100 --> 01:12:20.500
She's not in a good place.
她现在的状态很不好。

1313
01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:26.780
Jenna, there's a deleted scene that is so fantastic where you kind of whisper to Michael,
珍娜，有个删减片段太精彩了，你当时小声对迈克尔说，

1314
01:12:27.160 --> 01:12:27.900
go to Jan.
去找简。

1315
01:12:28.180 --> 01:12:29.460
Go comfort her.
去安慰她。

1316
01:12:29.700 --> 01:12:32.220
You kind of do this little motion, like, go say something.
你还做了个小动作，示意他去说点什么。

1317
01:12:32.220 --> 01:12:35.020
So he gets up and he walks over to her.
于是他起身走过去找她。

1318
01:12:35.160 --> 01:12:40.200
Again, he's comforting her, but we're all witness to it.
同样，他在安慰她，但我们都目睹了全过程。

1319
01:12:40.200 --> 01:12:44.120
And it's so clumsy and awkward.
那场面真是又笨拙又尴尬。

1320
01:12:44.940 --> 01:12:47.240
And Sam, can you play the first part of that?
山姆，你能播放那段的前半部分吗？

1321
01:12:48.320 --> 01:12:50.080
Hey, no, no, no.
嘿，不，不，不。

1322
01:12:50.180 --> 01:12:50.740
Don't be sad.
别难过。

1323
01:12:51.180 --> 01:12:51.980
Don't be sad.
别难过。

1324
01:12:53.080 --> 01:12:55.460
Look, I care about you and I support you.
听着，我在乎你，我也支持你。

1325
01:12:59.620 --> 01:13:02.160
You are smart and beautiful.
你既聪明又美丽。

1326
01:13:04.320 --> 01:13:06.300
And you have beautiful bosoMs.
而且你有一对漂亮的胸部。

1327
01:13:06.560 --> 01:13:09.500
And you can't even tell they're fake unless you're naked.
除非脱光了，否则根本看不出是假的。

1328
01:13:11.400 --> 01:13:17.480
And I believe that with my support and your constant calls to Dr. Perry on my phone plan,
我相信只要有我的支持，再加上你一直用我的手机套餐给佩里医生打电话，

1329
01:13:17.700 --> 01:13:22.920
which is a little bit of a strain because I only have 20 anytime minutes a month.
这确实有点吃力，因为我每个月只有20分钟的任意时段通话时长。

1330
01:13:23.700 --> 01:13:25.840
Every minute after that is 75 cents.
超出之后每分钟要75美分。

1331
01:13:26.780 --> 01:13:30.520
Oh, you should look at some other plans.
哦，你应该看看别的套餐。

1332
01:13:30.920 --> 01:13:32.740
Okay, thanks, weirdo.
好吧，谢谢你，怪胎。

1333
01:13:32.900 --> 01:13:33.580
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1334
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:36.060
I'm month to month because I don't want a two-year commitment.
我用的是月付套餐，因为我不想签两年的合约。

1335
01:13:37.700 --> 01:13:42.340
I remember when he turned to Beth and goes, oh, thanks, weirdo.
我记得他转向贝丝说：哦，谢谢你，怪胎。

1336
01:13:42.660 --> 01:13:44.300
We all lost it.
我们当时都笑疯了。

1337
01:13:44.860 --> 01:13:45.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1338
01:13:45.840 --> 01:13:48.520
Gene said that's one of his favorite lines that got cut.
吉恩说那是他最喜欢的被删台词之一。

1339
01:13:48.760 --> 01:13:49.660
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

1340
01:13:50.100 --> 01:13:50.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1341
01:13:50.520 --> 01:13:52.180
He loves that moment.
他很喜欢那一刻。

1342
01:13:52.820 --> 01:13:55.100
Michael continues to try to comfort Jan.
迈克尔继续试图安慰简。

1343
01:13:55.560 --> 01:14:01.500
And it doesn't get any better, but it really paints a picture of how he feels about his home life with her.
情况并没有好转，但这确实刻画了他对两人居家生活的真实感受。

1344
01:14:02.600 --> 01:14:03.940
What were you saying to Jan?
你当时对简说了什么？

1345
01:14:04.300 --> 01:14:10.640
Honey, nobody in the complex likes you, but you have made this place look great.
亲爱的，小区里没人喜欢你，但你把这儿布置得真棒。

1346
01:14:11.400 --> 01:14:12.760
It's like a museum.
简直像个博物馆。

1347
01:14:13.020 --> 01:14:13.300
Yeah.
是啊。

1348
01:14:13.300 --> 01:14:23.580
You can't touch anything, which is a really strange way to feel in the place that you live.
你什么都不能碰，在自己住的地方有这种感觉真的很奇怪。

1349
01:14:24.620 --> 01:14:28.100
You have made this home a house.
你把这个家变成了一座房子。

1350
01:14:29.660 --> 01:14:34.040
It's just what Paul Feig said about their design of the house.
这正是保罗·费格对他们房屋设计的评价。

1351
01:14:34.080 --> 01:14:34.700
Yes.
是的。

1352
01:14:34.880 --> 01:14:35.720
Like a museum.
就像个博物馆一样。

1353
01:14:36.040 --> 01:14:39.420
You have made this warm, cozy home a house.
你把这个温馨舒适的家变成了一座房子。

1354
01:14:41.260 --> 01:14:42.300
Oh, Michael.
噢，迈克尔。

1355
01:14:42.720 --> 01:14:52.720
I think they were right to leave those out because otherwise, I think we might have felt too badly for Jan when Michael is about to do what he's about to do.
我觉得他们没把那些剪掉是对的，否则的话，当迈克尔即将做出那种事时，我们可能会对简感到太同情了。

1356
01:14:52.720 --> 01:14:54.580
But before we get there, Angela,
但在那之前，安吉拉，

1357
01:14:54.840 --> 01:15:07.260
I have to talk about this moment when Dwight offers you some of his beet salad and you respond by saying the thought of popping one of his beets into your mouth makes you want to vomit.
我得聊聊那个瞬间，德怀特给你递了一些他的甜菜沙拉，而你回应说一想到要把他的甜菜塞进嘴里就想吐。

1358
01:15:08.120 --> 01:15:11.460
Because I remember something else that was happening during this scene.
因为我记得在那场戏拍摄期间还发生了别的事。

1359
01:15:11.560 --> 01:15:12.480
Will you share it with us?
你愿意和我们分享一下吗？

1360
01:15:12.980 --> 01:15:13.180
Yeah.
好的。

1361
01:15:13.520 --> 01:15:21.320
It was actually really hard for me to focus in this scene and say my dialogue because Jenna, my daughter in my belly,
其实在那场戏里我很难集中注意力说台词，因为珍娜，我肚子里的女儿，

1362
01:15:21.600 --> 01:15:24.660
just decided in that moment she was going to run a full marathon.
在那一刻决定要跑一场全程马拉松。

1363
01:15:24.960 --> 01:15:28.500
She was like, digg-a-dick, digg-a-dick, digg-a-dick, kicking so much.
她就像是在那儿踢啊踢，踢得特别厉害。

1364
01:15:28.640 --> 01:15:29.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

1365
01:15:29.280 --> 01:15:31.600
Maybe it's the sound of Rainn Wilson's voice.
也许是因为雷恩·威尔森的声音。

1366
01:15:32.340 --> 01:15:37.460
Maybe Rainn's voice awoken my child in my womb and she was ready to fight.
也许是雷恩的声音唤醒了我腹中的孩子，她准备好要打架了。

1367
01:15:37.760 --> 01:15:47.140
But it was so surreal to me to be thinking about the timing of the scene and everyone's dialogue and when I was supposed to come in and trying not to laugh.
但对我来说，一边要考虑戏的节奏和大家的台词，还要想我什么时候该出场，同时还要努力憋笑，这感觉太超现实了。

1368
01:15:47.340 --> 01:15:51.880
In the meantime, having this like wrestling match happening in my belly.
与此同时，我肚子里还在上演着一场摔跤比赛。

1369
01:15:52.120 --> 01:15:54.980
I think there are a lot of women who can relate to that, Angela.
我想很多女性都能感同身受，安吉拉。

1370
01:15:55.260 --> 01:16:00.080
I have a friend who is a lawyer and she was very, very pregnant and she was having to take a deposition.
我有个朋友是律师，她当时怀孕很深，不得不去参加一场取证会。

1371
01:16:00.080 --> 01:16:02.780
And she told me at the end of the day, she was like,
她告诉我，那天结束时，她说，

1372
01:16:02.920 --> 01:16:14.460
I could barely focus on what I was doing because I was having to give very carefully worded questions and comments because it was all going on the record.
我几乎无法专注于手头的工作，因为我必须给出措辞非常严谨的问题和评论，毕竟这些都要记录在案。

1373
01:16:14.620 --> 01:16:17.460
But all the while her kid in her belly was just tossing and turning.
但与此同时，她肚子里的孩子一直在翻来覆去。

1374
01:16:17.460 --> 01:16:19.980
Yeah, so much so.
是的，非常厉害。

1375
01:16:20.140 --> 01:16:23.520
And I have shared this story before and it's one of my favorite memories.
我以前分享过这个故事，这是我最珍贵的回忆之一。

1376
01:16:23.840 --> 01:16:30.380
While the scene was going on, I'm talking, everyone is saying their lines and there's the rapid cadence of the dialogue.
当那场戏正在进行时，我在说话，大家都在说台词，对话节奏很快。

1377
01:16:30.380 --> 01:16:44.440
I, off camera, grabbed Ed's hand and under the table, put it on my belly and he turned to me with his eyes wide and all of a sudden he wasn't Andy, he was Ed.
在镜头外，我抓住了艾德的手，放在了我的肚子上，他转过头看着我，眼睛瞪得大大的，那一刻他不再是安迪，他是艾德。

1378
01:16:44.600 --> 01:16:54.580
And he mouthed to me, oh my gosh, someone else to know and to witness like what I was like going through in the moment.
他对我做口型说，天哪，终于有另一个人知道并见证了我当时正在经历的一切。

1379
01:16:54.580 --> 01:16:56.920
And it's such a special memory to me.
这对我是非常特别的回忆。

1380
01:16:57.020 --> 01:17:03.800
And when I rewatched the episode with my daughter, I said, Isabel, you were running a marathon in mommy's belly right now.
当我后来和女儿重温这一集时，我说，伊莎贝尔，你当时就在妈妈肚子里跑马拉松呢。

1381
01:17:03.920 --> 01:17:04.800
And she was like, what?
她就说，什么？

1382
01:17:05.380 --> 01:17:06.840
It's so special to me.
这对我来说太特别了。

1383
01:17:07.300 --> 01:17:09.240
Guys, women are warriors.
伙计们，女性都是战士。

1384
01:17:09.980 --> 01:17:14.820
We go to work and we focus on our work as if we don't have that going on.
我们去工作，专注于工作，就好像我们没经历那些一样。

1385
01:17:15.220 --> 01:17:22.140
Try to imagine how I could put it to a man like, OK, you're trying to give the most important presentation of your life.
试着想象一下我该怎么跟男人解释，好吧，你正试图做人生中最重要的演讲。

1386
01:17:22.140 --> 01:17:25.120
And imagine a puppy is jumping at your leg the whole time.
想象一下有一只小狗一直在抓你的腿。

1387
01:17:25.360 --> 01:17:28.180
Like, just the most distracting thing.
就像，最让人分心的事情。

1388
01:17:28.540 --> 01:17:32.240
Jumping at your leg, but it's inside you, which is even weirder.
一直在抓你的腿，但它是在你身体里面，这就更诡异了。

1389
01:17:32.760 --> 01:17:33.120
Yeah.
是的。

1390
01:17:33.400 --> 01:17:34.600
It's like the alien.
就像异形一样。

1391
01:17:34.600 --> 01:17:35.520
What is happening?
这到底是怎么回事？

1392
01:17:35.900 --> 01:17:37.000
Women are warriors.
女性都是战士。

1393
01:17:37.580 --> 01:17:38.500
Way to go, Ange.
干得好，安吉。

1394
01:17:38.980 --> 01:17:43.240
Beth Grant also shared her memories about shooting this dinner table scene.
贝丝·格兰特也分享了她拍摄这场餐桌戏的回忆。

1395
01:17:43.460 --> 01:17:44.560
Let's have a listen.
让我们来听听。

1396
01:17:45.060 --> 01:17:48.480
Sitting at that table and, you know, sucking on those beats.
坐在那张桌子旁，你知道，吮吸着那些甜菜。

1397
01:17:48.720 --> 01:17:51.540
The reason I was sucking on those beats was to keep from laughing.
我吮吸那些甜菜的原因是为了忍住不笑。

1398
01:17:52.140 --> 01:17:57.520
And Rain's over there eating and going, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm.
而雷恩在那边吃着，发出嗯、嗯、嗯、嗯、嗯、嗯的声音。

1399
01:17:57.640 --> 01:18:01.680
There's so much subtle humor in this episode.
这一集里有太多微妙的幽默了。

1400
01:18:01.680 --> 01:18:05.540
And then, of course, the demented relationship that they have.
当然，还有他们之间那种扭曲的关系。

1401
01:18:05.680 --> 01:18:07.280
I love you all so much.
我非常爱你们大家。

1402
01:18:07.280 --> 01:18:12.400
I'm so honored to be part of this very popular and respected episode.
能参与这一集如此受欢迎且备受推崇的剧集，我深感荣幸。

1403
01:18:12.540 --> 01:18:17.500
Each of you doing such beautiful, subtle, hilarious comedy.
你们每个人都贡献了如此精彩、细腻且令人捧腹的喜剧表演。

1404
01:18:17.500 --> 01:18:20.800
And I was so thrilled to see that all of you broke up, too.
而且我很高兴看到你们也都笑场了。

1405
01:18:20.940 --> 01:18:25.280
Once we got inside and we sat down at the table and someone would break and say, sorry,
我们一进去坐到桌边，只要有人笑场说“抱歉”，

1406
01:18:25.480 --> 01:18:25.700
sorry.
抱歉。

1407
01:18:25.860 --> 01:18:26.960
And then someone else would break.
然后另一个人也会跟着笑场。

1408
01:18:27.160 --> 01:18:27.900
Sorry, sorry.
抱歉，抱歉。

1409
01:18:28.060 --> 01:18:28.980
And then we'd keep going.
然后我们再继续拍。

1410
01:18:29.280 --> 01:18:34.060
The last thing I'll say is when I came home, I said, I do not know how Paul is going to
最后我想说的是，当我回到家时，我说，我真不知道保罗要怎么

1411
01:18:34.060 --> 01:18:35.060
edit this.
剪辑这一集。

1412
01:18:35.500 --> 01:18:36.740
It's too hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1413
01:18:37.180 --> 01:18:39.180
Every moment is a three-hour episode.
每一刻都像是一部长达三小时的剧集。

1414
01:18:39.180 --> 01:18:41.240
I don't understand how he's going to do it.
我不明白他要怎么剪。

1415
01:18:41.360 --> 01:18:43.060
But by golly, you did it.
但天哪，你真的做到了。

1416
01:18:43.260 --> 01:18:50.200
And it is just an honor to have been part of this amazing, and as I say again, demented
能参与这一集精彩绝伦，正如我刚才所说，疯狂的

1417
01:18:50.200 --> 01:18:51.200
episode.
剧集，真是我的荣幸。

1418
01:18:54.220 --> 01:18:55.540
Amazing and demented.
精彩又疯狂。

1419
01:18:56.620 --> 01:18:58.020
That sums it up.
这就是最好的总结。

1420
01:18:58.240 --> 01:18:58.380
Yeah.
没错。

1421
01:18:58.840 --> 01:19:04.500
Gene told me that he and Lee actually begged NBC to make this a supersized episode.
吉恩告诉我，他和李其实曾恳求NBC把这一集做成超长版。

1422
01:19:04.500 --> 01:19:07.580
But I guess the schedule had already been set.
但我猜播出时间表已经定好了。

1423
01:19:07.760 --> 01:19:15.160
But he also told me that they did end up releasing a 29-minute producer's cut on iTunes that included
但他还告诉我，他们最终确实在iTunes上发布了一个29分钟的制片人剪辑版，其中包含了

1424
01:19:15.160 --> 01:19:19.640
a bunch of deleted scenes, including some of the ones we talked about, like the granola
一大堆删减片段，包括我们提到过的一些，比如燕麦棒

1425
01:19:19.640 --> 01:19:20.220
bar scene.
那一幕。

1426
01:19:20.420 --> 01:19:25.120
Maybe NBC didn't supersize it because they were holding a grudge because Greg wanted it to
也许NBC没有把它做成超长版是因为他们怀恨在心，因为格雷格想让它

1427
